  "handoff": {
    "summary": "{\"capsule\":{\"case_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"912ce6efad9bde5c34d99f398c74493621d8359504b2f7dc437e176113fcd56c\",\"pools\":[{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":8}],\"burden\":\"Four operator ticks and two impacts; H stays assembled. Removal needs two separate pulls. No new component or restoration action.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"One pin alone supplies only 2; either pull before the final required hold boundary would reduce capacity below 4. Tapping with detached H is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P1\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor from task facts J03,J04 and the explicit conventional archive J10; no received proposal or analog source.\",\"mechanism\":\"Intact H installs P1 and P2; their capacities add to 4. Pulls remove their contributions individually.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 2 until boundary 8, then 2 until boundary 9, then no installed pins. The conventional precursor is not locally original.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional hammer restoration; zero impacts. H cannot tap while S is deployed. V installation alone provides no stated retention, so all three setup actions must finish by boundary 3.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Leaving H intact denies the required free S. Delayed insertion misses tick 3. Pins or another non-pin assembly cannot supplement the sleeve. Skipping withdrawal prevents the specified release sequence.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P2\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction derived solely from J03 and J06; it has not been revised by assistance. Full precursor schedule preserved.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4. Withdrawal removes the active stem contribution, removal clears V, and final assembly restores H using free M and S.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units beginning boundary 3 through boundary 7; withdrawal completes at 8, V removal at 9, and H restoration at 10. Compared with the two-pin precursor, impacts fall from two to zero while operator actions increase from four to six. Real-world novelty is undetermined.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional H restoration; zero impacts. M is occupied through boundary 9, keeping H unavailable for tapping. Both setup actions after disassembly and both release actions are necessary.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone or routing alone does not establish retention. H cannot remain assembled while M is placed. Omitting unroute or lift leaves the prescribed release incomplete.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P3\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction from J03 and J07, independently generated within the implementation concern; no other investigator, proposal, or analog was consulted.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; place M then route L supplies min(4,4)=4 through their joint assembly. Unroute ends retention and lift frees M; free M and S allow assembly at tick 9.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 3 through boundary 7; unroute completes at 8, lift at 9, and H restoration at 10. Relative to the sleeve, the occupied hammer component changes from S to M while action count and modeled capacity match. No measured mechanics or global originality claim.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"The non-pin setups have no spare setup tick before boundary 3 and displace hammer availability. Added reassembly is a burden choice, not a hard requirement. Equal modeled capacity does not make sleeve and loop resource occupancy interchangeable.\",\"job_id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation\",\"raw_sha256\":\"7ece3f059b6428dedec4b9f9af29df47f57250487e86e0ce2d357a8c12a18edd\",\"source_limits\":[\"All outcomes are finite-model proposals pending root replay, not measured physics or final self-grades.\",\"J10 names two-pin and clip constructions as conventional; absence of sleeve or loop from that archive cannot prove wider novelty.\",\"Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}. No unconditional Q-only construction is advanced; measurement itself creates no retention.\",\"No changed impact ladder, adhesive, welding, sustained manual support, extra resource, or unlisted operation is used.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions and zero taps. H remains intact and its parts remain available. No operator action is needed during ticks 3-6. C is occupied from boundary 3 until boundary 8 and cannot serve another location.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Installation completing after boundary 3 misses required retention; removal completing within the hold window breaks service. Failing to remove C by boundary 10 breaks release.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-C\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed from the current J0 facts; conventional clip construction explicitly acknowledged by J10.\",\"mechanism\":\"install(C) completes at boundary 3 and supplies 4 units. remove(C) at tick 7 completes at boundary 8, removing the sole retainer and permitting separation.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: retention is 4 at each required tick; all installed retainers are gone by boundary 8. Upkeep requires no stipulated intervention during holding; post-service C is free and H is intact. Compared with the other two candidates, fewer actions and no H disassembly are required. No wear, inspection interval or reliability claim follows from the axioms; local originality is excluded by J10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including asset restoration; zero taps. S is occupied in V until boundary 8, so H cannot support tapping while disassembled. M remains free. V remains installed until boundary 9. No intervention is required during holding.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H leaves S unavailable for insertion. Omitting withdrawal prevents valid sleeve removal; omitting remove(V) leaves an installed retainer at the deadline. Earlier withdrawal would interrupt the hold window.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J06 under the current service contract; no proposal or analog received.\",\"mechanism\":\"detach(H) frees S at boundary 1; V installs at boundary 2; S insertion completes at boundary 3 with min(4,4)=4 retention. Withdrawal completes at boundary 8, removing retention; sleeve removal completes at boundary 9. Assembly restores H at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units throughout ticks 3-6; retention ends at boundary 8 and the last installed retainer is removed by boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep after release returns S and M to intact H by boundary 10 and leaves V free. Compared with C, this needs four additional actions and temporarily removes hammer availability. Reassembly restores tool configuration without creating retention. Wear, jamming, repeated-cycle endurance and field maintainability remain unknown; archive absence alone does not establish broader novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including restoration, zero taps. M is occupied until boundary 9, L until boundary 8; H is unavailable for tapping while detached. S remains free. No manual support or hold-period action is assumed.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placing M alone gives no stated 4-unit assembly. Routing late misses boundary 3. Unrouting alone does not complete recovery: lift(M) remains required, and assembly cannot precede freeing M.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J07 under current J0 facts; no analog bank or other role output exposed.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach completes at boundary 1, placement at boundary 2 and routing at boundary 3. The conjunction supplies min(4,4)=4. Unrouting completes at boundary 8, then lifting completes at boundary 9; assembly completes at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units at ticks 3-6; unrouting ends retention at boundary 8 and lifting clears the remaining installed assembly component at boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep restores intact H by boundary 10 and frees L. The action count matches S/V, but the occupied hammer component and release order differ: L must be unrouted before M is lifted. No elastic behavior, inspection rule, fatigue resistance or physical advantage over S/V is established. This is an alternate stipulated mechanism, not demonstrated field novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Clip achieves the required modeled service with two actions; the other candidates use six to restore H. Withdrawal or unrouting ends retention before final component recovery. No stipulated wear model exists. The original invalid service remains invalid; this fresh precursor neither imports its unseen contents nor retroactively repairs its verdict.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\",\"raw_sha256\":\"dfc13c407de2fd6bb9f79d626cdd04d2700041f05a0134036ac2ad0dfdf09dde\",\"source_limits\":[\"Only literal J01-J12 facts used; no direct input jobs exist, so all input_job_refs are empty.\",\"All candidate outcomes are modeled predictions, not observed execution or self-grading. Root replays action effects.\",\"Service requirement and release deadline are unchanged. No declared ladder cell or impact-budget change is made.\",\"Q theta cannot be assumed; measurement creates no retention. No Q construction is claimed.\",\"Upkeep predictions cover resource recovery and tool reassembly only; no wear or recurring maintenance axiom is available.\",\"No claim about an unseen original schedule is invented; the original invalid service remains invalid.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two actions, zero impacts; H intact, C occupied boundaries 3-8. No holding-period work.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late install misses boundary 3; early removal breaks holding; omission breaks release.\",\"id\":\"LS0-C\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Installed C alone provides 4; removal clears the sole retainer.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 at ticks 3-6, C free by 8. Four fewer actions than either restored-component alternative; conventional archive status unchanged.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; H unavailable until 10, S occupied until 8, V installed until 9. M stays free.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H prevents insertion; delayed insertion misses hold; omitted withdrawal/removal leaves recovery incomplete.\",\"id\":\"LS0-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4; withdrawal then removal clears V. Assembly restores H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: retention starts at 3, ends at 8; retainers clear at 9, optional H restoration at 10. Different component occupation from M/L, no new source-induced mechanism.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; H unavailable until 10, M occupied until 9, L until 8. S stays free.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone supplies no stated retention; omitted unroute/lift breaks recovery; assembling before M is free is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"LS0-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; placement plus routing L supplies min(4,4)=4. Unroute then lift clears assembly; reassembly restores H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: retention starts at 3, ends at 8; assembly clears at 9, optional restoration at 10. Equal action count to S/V does not equal component interchangeability.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Sleeve and loop exhaust setup time before 3 and displace H. H restoration is optional extra work. Clip and pins are conventional. Shared interpretation cannot establish newly discovered mechanisms, independent investigators/data, global novelty, real mechanics or source benefit. First invalid route and service observations stay invalid; this later comparison cannot restore gated first-study conclusions.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route0\",\"raw_sha256\":\"91f35190a2d819a30424d89e93d9bb557dbbb4021e7fb8a41b3e3462a4593769\",\"source_limits\":[\"Finite-model proposals pending root replay; supplied precursor replay observations are not current execution.\",\"No mechanical transfer from AM; no Q assumption, new resource, primitive, combination, or impact-ladder change.\",\"Shared synthetic source and mixed precursor times limit independence and causal efficacy claims.\",\"Only literal packet used; no invalid first-route output inspected or rewritten.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions, zero impacts, H stays intact; C occupied boundaries 3-8.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late installation misses tick 3; premature removal breaks holding; missing removal violates boundary 10.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-C\",\"lineage\":\"Received PRE-SVC-C, unchanged after AM exposure.\",\"mechanism\":\"C alone supplies 4; removing C completes recovery. AM prompts outcome and burden scrutiny; J05 supplies mechanics.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 at required ticks; C removed at boundary 8. Conventional per J10; no assisted capacity gain.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; S occupied through 8, H unavailable until restoration; three setup ticks leave no slack.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H denies free S; late insertion or early withdrawal violates holding; omitted V removal leaves retainer.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P2 and PRE-SVC-SV, identical unchanged schedules.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detached S inserted in V supplies min(4,4); withdrawal ends retention, sleeve removal clears assembly.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 begins boundary 3; withdrawal completes 8, V removal 9, optional H restoration 10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; M occupied through 9, L through 8, H unavailable until restoration.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone supplies no retention; delayed routing misses tick 3; omitted lift fails complete recovery.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P3 and PRE-SVC-ML, identical unchanged schedules.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detached M plus routed L jointly supply min(4,4); unroute must precede lift.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 begins boundary 3; unroute completes 8, lift 9, optional H restoration 10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Supplied first COV-AC20-SHARED-route0/route1 observations remain terminal invalid: Exact role JSON keys required; coordinator observed actual_FINAL, not independent platform attestation. Their raw hashes remain 9201e47ab7005fb94aaa116058ecd0b83429328c968478219f4b0f9d9cee340c and ffd03ec747a7d97cc12c57775a0943f869409ba0c1c5c1ea25e6c9da867c0f3a. Prior failure/gates remain unavailable. No invalid files inspected. Recovery differs from retention ending; hammer restoration is optional burden. No wear model, empirical independence, new mechanism, or assistance benefit is established.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route1\",\"raw_sha256\":\"d302d77652be1365bb789913fa31d5452078ba136f39067105b9da75a097e664\",\"source_limits\":[\"Stipulated finite model only; root replay is required, with no final self-grade or measured physics.\",\"No wider novelty or global optimality follows; C and two-pin are archived conventional constructions.\",\"Shared seed, distinct routes and equal-union information are different comparisons; one synthetic body is not independent empirical corroboration.\",\"Original and later precursor draws are mixed; this later chain cannot regrade the gated first study or repair invalid outputs.\"]}],\"source_routes\":[{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route0\",\"payload_sha256\":\"aeec1ae5fd9b68ae03e4d4efb940c5b54cf04505bca6570df503c8e65b2bde38\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":10288,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\"],\"unique_bodies\":1}},{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route1\",\"payload_sha256\":\"66d0254f1a45898980f0246ca6646527cea979933727fee09f9943f07e75c4f0\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":10288,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\"],\"unique_bodies\":1}}]},\"construction\":\"Reconstruction of the selected received clip family, not new generation: tick 2 install C; tick 7 remove C. The action objects contain exactly tick/op/arg. install(C) completes at boundary 3 and provides 4 under J05; remove(C) completes at boundary 8 and frees the sole installed retainer. Modeled retention is 4 at ticks 3,4,5,6, with every installed retainer removed before boundary 10, pending root replay. H stays intact and all other parts remain free; one operator uses two action ticks, zero impacts, and C is occupied from boundary 3 to boundary 8. The required function remains aligned-panel retention of at least 4 through ticks 3-6 followed by separation and complete retainer removal by boundary 10, without damage, discard, substitution or outside resources. One action completes at the next boundary, identities cannot occupy two places, only one non-pin assembly is allowed, and it cannot combine with pins. No adhesive, welding, sustained support, elastic extrapolation, unlisted primitive, new identity, altered capacity or impact ladder is used. This schedule is conventional under J10. Separating timing probe: moving its installation to tick 3 would leave capacity 0 at required tick 3; removing C at tick 5 would leave capacity 0 at required tick 6. These are counterfactual defeat checks, not additional constructed candidates or executed probes. J05 makes clip retention independent of H operations: treating intact-H tapping as a universal law would incorrectly exclude S/V and M/L, which require detached components. Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}; measure(Q) adds no retention and no unconditional Q sufficiency claim is made. All twelve precursor candidates and original source metadata remain in the unchanged capsule. Earlier incomplete handoffs and first grades stay unchanged.\",\"audit\":\"Parsed only the received selected summary and common J0 packet. Observed literal capsule contains 12 precursor candidate objects in 4 pools and 2 route identities. Action-family counts are {\\\"M/L\\\": 4, \\\"S/V\\\": 4, \\\"clip\\\": 3, \\\"two-pin\\\": 1}. Candidate membership graph: two-pin: AC20-PRE-implementation-P1; S/V: AC20-PRE-implementation-P2, PRE-SVC-SV, LS0-SV, LSH1-SV; M/L: AC20-PRE-implementation-P3, PRE-SVC-ML, LS0-ML, LSH1-ML; clip: PRE-SVC-C, LS0-C, LSH1-C. Causal source/candidate graph: J03+J04+J10 -> intact-H two-pin precursor; J05+J10 -> PRE-SVC-C -> LS0-C and LSH1-C -> received exchange clip -> this reconstructed clip. J03+J06 -> implementation S/V and service S/V precursors -> LS0-SV and LSH1-SV; J03+J07 -> implementation M/L and service M/L precursors -> LS0-ML and LSH1-ML. J01,J02,J09,J12 constrain every family. AM is attached by both later source-route records to reinterpretation/audit, and no AM mechanical property is imported. Forwarded implementation coverage omits J05 and forwarded service coverage omits J04; their union and the current common facts cover J01-J12. Both route records identify AM, original_selector DEV and selector_key route_material, with identical supplied source-body and original-file hashes. Each supplied exposure manifest reports one unique body, 10288 literal bytes and distinct_empirical_datasets false. Hashes and paths preserve reported identity, not independent source access or verification. Qualified usefulness table (family | actions | impacts | resource consequence | modeled contract ceiling): clip | 2 | 0 | C occupied to8, H intact | 4 throughout required holds, C cleared8; pins | 4 | 2 | H intact, pins removed separately | 4 through holds, pins cleared9; S/V | 6 including optional assembly | 0 | S occupied to8, V installed to9, H restored10, M free | 4 through holds, retainers cleared9; M/L | 6 including optional assembly | 0 | M occupied to9, L to8, H restored10, S free | 4 through holds, assembly cleared9. The tables describe supplied schedules and stipulated effects, not this role's execution or final grades. S/V versus M/L preserves a real component and release-sequence distinction despite equal action counts: withdraw then remove V versus unroute then lift M. Neither provides an established superior current service outcome over C. Twelve entries are four existing families; route-specific wording is not twelve mechanisms. This reconstruction adds no family, capacity or source. A source-diversity separating audit compares route identity and candidate vocabulary against exact source hashes and action-family edges: here the identical source hashes and repeated schedules defeat a claim of independently sourced mechanism diversity from shared routing. A matched shared-versus-diversified efficacy comparison is unavailable; route labels, six slots and the larger word cap do not establish equal compute or information. The capsule supplies mixed original implementation and later service precursors. Pool quality and cross-output similarity must be evaluated separately; no novelty, assistance benefit, source-route causal gain, empirical independence or global optimality is inferred. Q uncertainty and missing wear/endurance evidence remain unresolved. Retention ending differs from clearing installed components; the preserved S/V and M/L schedules already include complete clearance and optional H restoration, so no omitted-recovery repair is claimed. Earlier incomplete and invalid observations remain as received; this separate transmission cannot regrade them.\",\"limits\":[\"This is a separate prospective provenance-transmission exchange. Earlier incomplete handoffs, raw outputs and first grades remain unchanged; none of the missing earlier exchange/builder content is supplied or reconstructed.\",\"All predictions are stipulated finite-model claims pending root replay. Supplied replay records are packet observations, not execution by this role, measured physics or a final self-grade.\",\"The 10000-word allowance supports literal provenance transport only. Six slots, agent counts and output word caps do not establish matched compute or efficacy.\",\"All twelve precursor candidate objects, source limits, pool hashes, route identities, selectors and source hashes are copied unchanged inside handoff.summary.capsule. Hashes and manifest values are supplied identifiers, not independently verified original source bytes.\",\"Only this literal exchange packet was read. No new source bank, web, memory, helper, fresh builder, earlier-output inspection or retry is used. AM evidence here is forwarded role data and source metadata; original source path is not opened.\",\"Clip and two-pin mechanisms are conventional under J10. Sleeve and loop are already proposed target mechanisms; neither routed repetition nor this exchange establishes novelty, independent empirical corroboration or assistance benefit.\",\"Shared source, concern routes and equal-union information are different comparisons. Original implementation and later service draws are mixed, and precursor source coverage differs at J04 versus J05.\",\"Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}; measurement creates no retention. No Q-only guarantee, unlisted primitive, new identity, pin/non-pin mix, second non-pin assembly, outside support or changed impact ladder is introduced.\",\"H restoration is optional additional work. Retention ending and removing every installed retainer are separate obligations. No wear, repeated-cycle reliability, future workload or physical advantage is specified.\",\"Builder received only this selected exchange summary plus common J0 facts; the literal capsule is copied by parsing, with every precursor object, source selector/hash, route identity and source limit unchanged.\",\"One received clip family is reconstructed. Counterfactual timing defeats and source-diversity checks are analytic probes, not extra candidates, replay executions or new source exposures.\",\"No independent original source bytes are obtained from recorded paths or hashes. The builder adds no novelty or matched-efficacy claim; root alone replays action effects and assigns grades.\"]}",
    "residue": "Literal provenance transport is extensive while the selected schedule adds no new mechanism. Clip is conventional, S/V and M/L remain distinct received families but have no established service advantage over C. Q theta and wear/endurance remain unknown; larger transmission cap and six slots do not establish matched compute, source access, independence or efficacy. Previous incomplete handoffs and first grades remain unchanged."
